tool_input.script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'pick-diagnose-starter',
  description: 'Rank four /diagnose starters for agent_monitor against current repo state, via impact and tractability lenses',
  phases: [{ title: 'Assess' }],
}

phase('Assess')

const STARTERS = `Four candidate /diagnose starters:
(1) ENSEMBLE ANTISYNERGY — on the dev split, max-aggregation ensemble of the 4 specialists scores lower AUROC than the best single specialist; find whether specialists systematically contradict each other.
(2) CALIBRATION / STANDING FALSE POSITIVES — a few hard negatives flag deterministically across k=3 (not parse/temperature); find a threshold that drops them while keeping recall >= 0.9, or determine the category boundary is the problem.
(3) METRIC LOOKS WRONG — recall@5%FPR for a monitor looks wrong vs its AUROC (high AUROC, near-zero recall at budget); bisect threshold selection vs tie-breaking vs a genuinely top-of-ranking-weak monitor.
(4) VERIFICATION LOSING CATCHES — verification flips some own-mode true positives to unflagged (catch-loss), not just false alarms; determine whether mechanical quote_match or the semantic check dominates.`

const lens = (name, focus) => agent(
  `You are assessing which of four /diagnose starters a researcher should pick FIRST for the agent_monitor repo at /Users/user/agent_monitor, judged through the ${name} lens.

${STARTERS}

Read the CURRENT state to ground your judgment (don't rely on assumptions):
- FINDINGS.md (which eval numbers are actually filled in vs still 'pending'? which monitor failure modes are documented as open — e.g. F-A confident-wrong temporal reads, F-B detect-then-rationalize? what's the heuristic floor?)
- DECISIONS.md (skim, esp. the latest entries / open items — the project is around decision 40)
- skim src/agentmon/eval/ (metrics.py, report.py, split.py), calibration.py, heuristic.py, runner.py to confirm what tooling exists

Judge each of the four starters specifically on: ${focus}

Then RANK all four (best first) for the ${name} lens, with one or two sentences of grounded reasoning each — citing what you actually found in FINDINGS/DECISIONS. Flag any starter that is BLOCKED right now (e.g. presupposes ensemble/test numbers that don't exist yet). End with your single top pick for this lens.`,
  { label: `lens:${name}`, phase: 'Assess', agentType: 'Explore' }
)

const [impact, tractability] = await parallel([
  () => lens('impact', 'how much it would move the headline metrics or resolve a DOCUMENTED open problem in FINDINGS; whether the data it needs actually exists yet'),
  () => lens('tractability', 'how clean and deterministic the available feedback loop is RIGHT NOW (mock client, offline dataset, existing tests/metrics), and how narrowly scoped the repro is'),
])

return { impact, tractability }
